  "description": "streamed-forest made for the walk's stalls (roadmap T168): the same trees ten times over, 30,000 on a disc of 2 km, a streamed layer of solved boulders and stones under them to the last ring (up to 120 a tile), and the ground drawn from the world's tiles, so the walker stands on a tile source and its collision builds tiles ahead (scene_collision.md). A flight at hundreds of metres a second turns the tail over by tens of thousands of instances a second as a player's flight over the forest proof of concept does: it empties and fills, its tables grow, and a walker dropped from it fills its ring at once. fast-flight.json flies it; run-drop.jsonl replays a sprint, a flight and a drop, twice; README.md, 'The turnover variant', says what each reproduces.",
